If our product candidates are approved but fail to achieve market acceptance among physicians,
patients, hospitals, cancer treatment centers or others in the medical community, we will not be able to
generate significant revenue. Even if our drugs achieve market acceptance, we may not be able to maintain
that market acceptance over time if new products or technologies are introduced that are more favorably
received than our drugs, receive more favorable reimbursement, are more cost effective or render our drugs
obsolete.
